1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,880
What if a cat bit you, and instead of a trip to the doctor, you got actual cat powers?

2
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:05,872
Let's find out.

3
00:00:05,922 --> 00:00:09,802
Step one: pet a grumpy cat that has clearly, loudly, repeatedly said no.

4
00:00:10,169 --> 00:00:11,969
Chomp!

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:16,830
Quick reality check: in real life, a cat bite gives you an infection, not superpowers.

6
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,970
Cat teeth are tiny needles full of bacteria, so please, see a doctor.

7
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:22,577
But this is a what-if. So: day one.

8
00:00:22,627 --> 00:00:24,437
You wake up, look in the mirror, and… ears!

9
00:00:24,487 --> 00:00:27,023
Two brand new ears, right on top of your head.

10
00:00:27,073 --> 00:00:28,983
Also a tail. Nobody asked for the tail.

11
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:30,833
The tail is here anyway.

12
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:32,640
Power number one: night vision!

13
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:39,478
Cats can see in light about six times dimmer than you need, which is why they can sprint across a dark room without hitting anything.

14
00:00:39,528 --> 00:00:43,958
Behind the eye there's a mirror layer that bounces light back through the eye for a second try.

15
00:00:44,008 --> 00:00:46,468
That's also why cat eyes glow in photos.

16
00:00:46,688 --> 00:00:50,898
So at three in the morning, in total darkness, you can finally find the TV remote.

17
00:00:50,948 --> 00:00:52,748
True hero stuff.

18
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:55,940
Next up, power number two: you always land on your feet!

19
00:00:55,990 --> 00:00:59,740
Cats twist in mid-air: head first, then the front legs, then the back, like a spring unwinding.

20
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:04,030
They can do it from a fall of about thirty centimeters, without even thinking.

21
00:01:04,434 --> 00:01:06,824
So you fall off a ladder? Ta-da! Perfect landing.

22
00:01:06,874 --> 00:01:08,674
The paint bucket? Not so lucky.

23
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:11,140
Power number three: the jump!

24
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:14,370
A cat can leap up to five times its own height in a single bounce.

25
00:01:14,562 --> 00:01:17,352
You're one point eight meters tall. Times five…

26
00:01:17,402 --> 00:01:18,372
that's nine meters.

27
00:01:18,422 --> 00:01:20,822
A two-story roof, from standing, with no run-up!

28
00:01:21,151 --> 00:01:22,951
Your neighbors have questions.

29
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:25,580
Power number four: super hearing!

30
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:28,900
Humans hear sounds up to about twenty thousand hertz. A cat?

31
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:30,560
Up to sixty-four thousand.

32
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:32,430
That's way past anything you've ever heard.

33
00:01:32,499 --> 00:01:37,029
So now you can hear a mouse in the walls, the neighbor's microwave, and your own fridge humming.

34
00:01:37,079 --> 00:01:38,879
All day. Every day.

35
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:40,960
Power number five: super reflexes!

36
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:42,860
You react in about a quarter of a second.

37
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:45,140
A cat reacts in twenty to seventy milliseconds.

38
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:47,070
That's faster than a blink.

39
00:01:47,154 --> 00:01:51,684
So your arch-enemy, Doctor Woof, sits down with your favorite food: a double cheeseburger.

40
00:01:51,734 --> 00:01:54,814
And before he can even say mine… the burger is gone.

41
00:01:55,157 --> 00:01:57,207
Thirty milliseconds. He didn't even see you move. Delicious.

42
00:01:57,257 --> 00:01:59,057
Justice!

43
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:02,275
But every hero has a weakness. Yours? A tiny red dot.

44
00:02:02,325 --> 00:02:05,895
Doctor Woof switches on a laser pointer, and your cat brain takes over.

45
00:02:05,945 --> 00:02:09,265
You chase it up the wall, across the floor, and straight into a lamp.

46
00:02:09,351 --> 00:02:13,751
Cats are wired to chase small, fast things, and that makes it really hard to focus.

47
00:02:14,051 --> 00:02:15,841
You were in the middle of saving the city.

48
00:02:15,891 --> 00:02:17,691
Now you are staring at a wall.

49
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:20,368
And cat powers come with cat habits.

50
00:02:20,418 --> 00:02:22,108
Habit one: things on edges must fall.

51
00:02:22,158 --> 00:02:24,488
Your boss's mug is right on the edge of the desk.

52
00:02:24,538 --> 00:02:26,478
You look at it. It looks at you.

53
00:02:27,458 --> 00:02:28,568
You don't know why you did it.

54
00:02:28,618 --> 00:02:30,418
You would absolutely do it again.

55
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:33,220
Habit two: cats can't taste sweet.

56
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:36,000
The sweet-taste gene is broken, so birthday cake now tastes like…

57
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:37,850
wet bread.

58
00:02:38,650 --> 00:02:41,260
And the big one: cats sleep twelve to sixteen hours a day.

59
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:42,194
So do you now.

60
00:02:42,244 --> 00:02:44,054
A superhero shift is eight hours.

61
00:02:44,104 --> 00:02:46,004
You are awake for eight hours. Total.

62
00:02:46,098 --> 00:02:47,728
The city calls for Meow Man.

63
00:02:47,778 --> 00:02:50,718
Meow Man is in a box, in a sunbeam. Do not disturb.

64
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,260
So, being a cat superhero?

65
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:55,360
Amazing powers, terrible schedule.

66
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:57,270
Next time: what if a dog licked you?
